touchpad: start the cursor and two-finger scrolling at once, and move the cursor evenly when slow.

With tap-to-click on, a finger that comes down is in TAP_STATE_TOUCH until it moves 1.3mm or 180ms
pass, and tp_tap_handle_state() filters all pointer motion meanwhile, never replaying it: the
cursor sits still for the first 1.3mm of every stroke. On the PX13's touchpad (PixArt 093A:3013)
that was ~100ms and ~15 logical px per quick stroke. Let it move the cursor at once instead: a tap
then moves the cursor by however far the finger wobbled, a pixel or two.

Slow cursor motion lurched: below 7mm/s the touchpad's acceleration slows the cursor down, to a
third at the slowest, by the speed it estimates, which is that of the last motion event alone. At
each slow start that estimate is near zero (a pause before), then jumps up, so the cursor sped up
~1.8x within 20-40ms while the finger moved steadily (a recording, 2026-11-10). Now it doesn't slow
down: the cursor moves as far for each mm at any speed up to the acceleration. Optionally, the
speed estimate can be averaged over time, pauses included.

Two-finger scrolling started late for three reasons:
- The same filter in TAP_STATE_TOUCH_2 (a possible two-finger tap). Dropped likewise.
- tp_gesture_detect_motion_gestures() waits for both fingers to move 1.5mm the same way (and
  doesn't look before one moved 1mm). Now 0.75mm (and 0.5mm). A pinch taken for a scroll is still
  corrected within 300ms.
- The motion before the scroll was recognized was dropped. Now the scroll makes up for it, not at
  once (the content would jump) but by scrolling faster than the fingers at first, easing back to
  their speed as it catches up.

Each is a setting, in the [Touchpad] group of ~/.config/danylo-tweaksrc (System Settings >
Danylo's Linux Tweaks > Touchpad), read again within a second of a change:
  MoveDuringTap=true         (false: libinput's filter for one finger)
  ScrollDuringTap=true       (false: and for two)
  ScrollStartDistance=0.75   (mm, libinput's is 1.5)
  ScrollDecideDistance=0.5   (mm, libinput's is 1)
  ScrollCatchUp=1            (the scroll's speed at first is 1 + this times the fingers', 0 drops
                             the motion as libinput does)
  SlowSpeedGain=1            (the cursor's speed at the slowest finger speeds, as a fraction of
                             its speed from 7mm/s: libinput's is 0.33)
  SpeedSmoothing=0           (ms over which the finger's speed is averaged, 0: libinput's estimate)

Applied by scripts/patches/patch-library, see scripts/configure_hardware.

